\section{Training Hyperparameters}
\label{sec:hyperparams}

Table~\ref{tab:hyperparams} lists the hyperparameters for all training configurations. All methods use LoRA with rank $r{=}64$ and $\alpha{=}128$ applied to attention projections. SFT and RSFT share the same optimizer settings; RSFT differs only in data construction (top-1 CED-selected outputs from $N{=}8$ candidates). GRPO and DPO use lower learning rates to stabilize post-SFT optimization.

\begin{table*}[t]
\centering
\caption{Training hyperparameters for all optimization paradigms. All experiments use Qwen3-4B as the base model with LoRA adaptation. A dash indicates that the parameter is not applicable to the given method.}
\label{tab:hyperparams}
\small
\begin{tabular}{lccccc}
\toprule
\textbf{Parameter} & \textbf{SFT} & \textbf{RSFT} & \textbf{GRPO QLoRA} & \textbf{GRPO bf16} & \textbf{DPO} \\
\midrule
Base model & Qwen3-4B & Qwen3-4B & Qwen3-4B & Qwen3-4B & Qwen3-4B \\
LoRA rank $r$ & 64 & 64 & 64 & 64 & 64 \\
LoRA $\alpha$ & 128 & 128 & 128 & 128 & 128 \\
Learning rate & 2e-5 & 2e-5 & 5e-6 & 5e-6 & 5e-7 \\
Batch size (effective) & 16 & 16 & 4 & 8 & 4 \\
Epochs & 3 & 1 & -- & -- & 1, 3\textsuperscript{$\star$} \\
Max steps & -- & -- & 100 & 100 & -- \\
Gradient accumulation & 4 & 4 & 16 & 4 & 4 \\
Max new tokens & 1024 & 1024 & 1024 & 1024 & 1024 \\
Quantization & -- & -- & NF4 4-bit & bf16 & bf16 \\
Group size $G$ & -- & -- & 4 & 8 & -- \\
KL coefficient & -- & -- & 0.01 & 0.01 & -- \\
$\beta$ (DPO) & -- & -- & -- & -- & 0.1 \\
Candidates $N$ & -- & 8 & -- & -- & 8 \\
Top-$k$ selection & -- & 1 & -- & -- & -- \\
Training samples & 3,053 & 2,718 & 3,053 & 3,053 & 3,053 \\
Scoring function & -- & CED & CED & CED & CED \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\vspace{1mm}
{\raggedright\footnotesize \textsuperscript{$\star$}DPO is trained for both 1 and 3 epochs to observe temporal dynamics of the evidence-extraction trade-off (Section~\ref{sec:spectrum}).\par}
\end{table*}


\section{Full Ablation Results}
\label{sec:ablation_full}

Table~\ref{tab:ablation_full} reports the complete RSFT ablation across scoring functions, top-$k$ values, and random seeds. RSFT CED $k{=}1$ achieves a mean Ign-F1 of 44.66 with low variance across four seeds (standard deviation 0.49), confirming the robustness of the improvement over the SFT baseline (39.74). Increasing $k$ to 3 slightly degrades performance (43.64 Ign-F1), consistent with the intuition that stricter selection yields higher-quality training data. The flat-NLI scoring variant produces comparable Rel-F1 (mean 0.4561 vs.\ 0.4563 for CED, a difference of 0.02pp). Both CED and flat-NLI improve substantially over the SFT baseline while maintaining or improving Evi-F1, confirming that the RSFT gains are driven by quality-based data selection rather than by the specific contrastive formulation.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\caption{Full RSFT ablation on DocRED dev set (Qwen3-4B). CED and flat-NLI denote the scoring function used for candidate selection. Best Ign-F1 among evidence-generating methods in \textbf{bold}.}
\label{tab:ablation_full}
\small
\begin{tabular}{lcccc}
\toprule
\textbf{Configuration} & \textbf{Ign-F1} & \textbf{Rel-F1} & \textbf{Evi-F1} & \textbf{EDCR} \\
\midrule
SFT baseline & 39.74 & 0.4049 & 79.86 & 0.6982 \\
SFT no-evidence & \textbf{47.21} & 0.4876 & -- & -- \\
\midrule
RSFT CED $k{=}1$ (s42) & 44.23 & 0.4517 & 81.75 & 0.6569 \\
RSFT CED $k{=}1$ (s43) & 45.12 & 0.4601 & 80.87 & 0.6521 \\
RSFT CED $k{=}1$ (s44) & 45.11 & 0.4621 & 80.50 & 0.6350 \\
RSFT CED $k{=}1$ (s45) & 44.16 & 0.4514 & 81.74 & 0.6550 \\
RSFT CED $k{=}1$ (mean) & 44.66 & 0.4563 & 81.22 & 0.6498 \\
\midrule
RSFT CED $k{=}3$ & 43.64 & 0.4454 & 80.88 & 0.6635 \\
\midrule
RSFT flat-NLI (s42) & -- & 0.4535 & 80.43 & 0.6431 \\
RSFT flat-NLI (s43) & -- & 0.4586 & 81.58 & 0.6505 \\
RSFT flat-NLI (mean) & -- & 0.4561 & 81.01 & 0.6468 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}


\section{Scaling Details}
\label{sec:scaling_details}

Table~\ref{tab:cross_detail} supplements Table~\ref{tab:scaling} in the main text with per-scale Rel-F1 and Evi-F1 breakdowns. At 1.7B, RSFT improves Rel-F1 from 0.4945 to 0.5219 (+0.0274) while achieving Evi-F1 83.09. The 4B model shows the same pattern at a larger magnitude: Rel-F1 increases from 0.4049 to 0.4563 (+0.0514, four-seed mean). For 8B, RSFT brings Rel-F1 from 0.5262 to 0.5606 with Evi-F1 of 80.52 and EDCR 0.6377, confirming tight coupling between extraction and evidence at this scale.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\caption{Detailed Rel-F1 and Evi-F1 across model scales on DocRED dev set. SFT columns show the joint-evidence baseline; RSFT columns show CED $k{=}1$ four-seed mean for 4B, single seed for other scales. Dashes indicate metrics not computed at that scale (evidence evaluation infrastructure was not available for 1.7B/8B SFT at submission time).}
\label{tab:cross_detail}
\small
\begin{tabular}{lccccc}
\toprule
\textbf{Model} & \textbf{SFT Rel-F1} & \textbf{SFT Evi-F1} & \textbf{RSFT Rel-F1} & \textbf{RSFT Evi-F1} & \textbf{RSFT EDCR} \\
\midrule
Qwen3-1.7B & 0.4945 & -- & 0.5219 & 83.09 & -- \\
Qwen3-4B & 0.4049 & 79.86 & 0.4563 & 81.22 & 0.6498 \\
Qwen3-8B & 0.5262 & -- & 0.5606 & 80.52 & 0.6377 \\
LLaMA-3.1-8B & 0.5514 & 81.51 & \texttt{TBD} & \texttt{TBD} & \texttt{TBD} \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}


\section{GRPO Training Dynamics}
\label{sec:grpo_dynamics}

\begin{figure*}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{fig_grpo_dynamics.pdf}
\caption{Training dynamics of GRPO under different configurations. (a)~Relation F1 across checkpoints: G=4 QLoRA suffers catastrophic collapse at step~10, while G=8 bf16 remains stable. (b)~Evidence F1 stays intact for G=8 bf16, confirming the generation mechanism itself does not fail. (c)~Evidence-Decoupling Ratio (EDCR) reveals near-total decoupling in G=4 QLoRA (citations redirect to distractors), while G=8 bf16 maintains healthy ratios.}
\label{fig:grpo_dynamics}
\end{figure*}

